{"title":"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The discriminant of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133a027883f1518cefa76684483cf81206bfd3d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+2x\\sqrt{3}+3=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> is zero. Hence, its roots are: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/671b3e9b910cb58035eb3e36b974dcbc9222cc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{real and equal}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{rational and equal}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{rational and unequal}\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{irrational and unequal}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{imaginary}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"555\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the discriminant is zero, there is one distinct root, or, relevant to this question, two equal roots. The fact that only one solution exists means that the equation can be simplified into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484d536d335dfaace71bf96fd2acd0dd7cbac940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + \\sqrt{3})^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"21\" />. The distinct solution^ to the equation, as we can clearly see, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4bf8757013ec8c2feb63034e350c3ce9985f67e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"21\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3c8fd76dd1ef42537c46da1c272bd5136311a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\text{real and equal}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>^The problem pretends to have two solutions.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME\" title=\"1955 AHSME\">1955 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1955 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1955\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title